# Antigravity Rules - Cross-Platform Execution & Performance

## Shell Execution
- Windows OS: Always use 'cmd /c' for shell executions to ensure processes terminate cleanly and send proper EOF signals.
- macOS / Linux OS: Run commands directly in the default shell (bash/zsh) with non-interactive flags where appropriate.
- Avoid hanging interactive shell sessions or unbuffered long-running loops without timeouts.

## Workspace & Monorepo Guidance
- This project is a monorepo containing `backend`, `frontend`, `mobile`, `infra`, and `bot-simulator`.
- Refer to `package.json` and dependency manifests for packages; do not scan or index files inside `node_modules` or build directories.
